{1 = 1-2}
9=1.	Say to my lord: this is what @wPN{Aradŋu}, 
13=2.	your servant, says: 

{3 = 3-8}
17=3.	You instructed me, as I was taking the direct route to @wGN{Subir}, 
21=4.	to secure your provincial taxes, 
25=5.	to inform myself precisely as to the state of the territory, 
29=6.	and to ensure its obedience by taking counsel with (?) @wPN{Apillaša}, 
33=7.	the 'Sage of the Assembly', 
37=8.	so that he could thus return the people of @wGN{Subir} to their customary way of speaking (?). 

{9 = 9-11}
41=9.	But when I arrived at the palace gate, no one enquired after the well-being of my lord. 
45=10.	No one rose from their seat before me, or bowed down. 
49=11.	@vart[t3101.v1,t3101.v1]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} They intimidated me. } 

{12 = 12-18}
56=12.	@varh[t3101.v2]{When I came nearer } @vart[t3101.v3,t3101.v2]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… carries …… } -- well, 
63=13.	your wayside hostel where carding-combs (?) and lances inlaid with gold, 
67=14.	silver, cornelian and lapis lazuli have been set up, 
71=15.	covers an area of one hectare! 
78=16.	@wPN{Apillaša} himself is decked out in @varh[t3101.v4]{gold and lapis lazuli } @vart[t3101.v5,t3101.v4]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} lapis lazuli, gold, silver and cornelian }, and he sits on a raised throne furnished with a rich raiment. 
82=17.	His feet rest upon a golden footstool. 
86=18.	He would not remove his feet in my presence! 

{19 = 19-21}
90=19.	To his right and left he had …… soldiers (?) stationed, five thousand at each side. 
94=20.	He placed at their disposal six fattened oxen and @varh[t3101.v6]{60 } @vart[t3101.v7,t3101.v6]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} 20 } fattened @varh[t3101.v8]{sheep } @vart[t3101.v9,t3101.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} rams } for a meal. 
103=21.	He assumed the right to perform my lord's lustration rites. 

{22 = 22-25}
107=22.	After a close interrogation at the gate, nobody even bade me enter. 
111=23.	When I finally entered, someone brought me a throne with studs plated with red gold and told me: 
115=24.	@q[someone,Aradju]{“Sit down!”} I replied: 
119=25.	@q[Aradju,someone]{“I am here to present the instructions of my king. Therefore I will not sit down!"”} 

{26 = 26-28}
123=26.	They brought (?) me @varh[t3101.v10]{two fattened oxen } @vart[t3101.v11,t3101.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} one fattened ox } and @varh[t3101.v12]{20 } @vart[t3101.v13,t3101.v12]{@varn{the same ms. has instead:} 6 } fattened sheep to my table. 
132=27.	Then because, without ……, my lord's soldiers overturned my table, 
136=28.	I became frightened and my flesh crept. 

{29 = 29-34}
140=29.	In the month Ezen-Ninazu, 
149=30.	after @varh[t3101.v14]{the 15th day } @vart[t3101.v15,t3101.v14]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} five days had passed }, my lord gave me his instructions. 
153=31.	@varh[t3101.v16]{By the first day } @vart[t3101.v17,t3101.v16]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} after one day had passed } of the month U-bigu, 
